FORECAST (labelled; optimistic): 3 sigma needs ~2.71e+05 CFHTLenS-like pairs (x12); a ~100x pair sample with ~2x source density gives S/N ~ 12.4
REPORTED: AG6C's mid-plane column through the saddle (grid h) is negative part -0.2064 but NET +0.0160 (dimensionless);
  at the primary values that is -0.203 and +0.016 Msun/pc^2. AQUAL's own projected column through the saddle is
  POSITIVE: neither model predicts negative convergence there. The separating signal is a dip of depth ~|negative part| in the
  positive bridge (AQUAL) versus no dip (a medium that cannot go below zero, if it keeps the positive part). That is what (a)/(b) size.
REPORTED: field in the mid-plane at R = 0.2 d (primary pair, superposed deep-MOND estimate): g ~ 2.3e-03 a0.
Not included (each weakens the test): any external field above that fills the null point (not modelled); the dip's real profile
  (thinner than the 0.1 d strip, and smeared for pairs not seen edge-on); the d = 6 h-1 Mpc bracket keeps all 23,000 pairs; correlated
  Kaiser-Squires noise; the positive filament and the medium's own departure from the law, which must be modelled to isolate the dip.
